    "productVersion": "1.0.0-beta.3",
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-08 13:11:44",
    "releaseNotes": "# AID v1.0.0-beta.3 测试版\n\n## 中文更新说明\n\n- 新增官方资产状态检查与导入能力，完善 OSS 配置、连通性检测、媒体地址解析和上传限制处理。\n- 文件存储开箱即用：首次初始化默认启用本地存储，本地模式只需一个可选站点域名，官方资源路径自动映射到 `/profile/aid/...`，不再要求重复填写 CDN 域名。\n- RocketMQ 默认完全关闭；只有部署配置显式开启基础设施且后台业务开关同时开启时才使用 MQ，未配置环境不会初始化生产者或消费者。\n- 完善错误日志与错误规则转换流程，提升后台定位供应商异常和维护错误规则的效率。\n- 重构项目升级管理页面，优化版本状态、升级器状态、发布说明、运行配置和官方资产信息的展示布局。\n- 完善项目升级配置中心：Docker 与非 Docker 配置分区管理，支持在后台配置 HTTPS 用户域名、管理域名及端口，并安全上传证书链与私钥。\n- 新增 DNS、证书、HTTPS、MySQL、Redis、RocketMQ 等逐项诊断；证书写入前校验域名、有效期、用途和密钥匹配，并自动保留受控备份用于恢复。\n- 新增升级/回退实时终端、阶段进度和 `aid progress` 命令，并在页面、服务端与安装脚本三层阻止重复升级任务。\n- 在线升级前自动检测服务器 CPU 与内存；CPU 不超过 4 核或内存不超过 4 GiB 时展示宕机风险与备份确认。\n- 修复 Docker 首次部署时升级器配置可能落入临时目录的问题；旧配置会在严格校验后安全迁移到受控目录，并保留备份。\n- Docker 与非 Docker 后端运行环境统一固定 UTF-8，修复官方资产包内中文对象键无法在 Linux 初始化的问题。\n- 完善非 Docker 部署下受管 Redis 客户端识别，以及同版本升级器制品刷新和自愈逻辑。\n- 优化剧集审核流程：成品视频与剧集描述仍为必填，剧集封面调整为选填；填写封面时继续校验地址有效性。\n- 优化 Web 创作流程，包括成片预览与发布、电影/剧集状态隔离、生成模型参数同步、分镜任务刷新恢复、视频时长识别、字幕展示和批量生成参数过滤。\n- 随版本提供 `sql/v1.0.0-beta.3.sql` 增量脚本；升级器会按既有升级记录机制执行，升级前请先备份数据库和部署配置。\n\n\u003e 本版本为 Beta 测试版，建议先在测试环境验证模型配置、对象存储、数据库升级和创作全流程后再用于生产环境。\n\n# AID v1.0.0-beta.3 Beta Release\n\n## English Release Notes\n\n- Added official asset status checks and import support, with improved OSS configuration, connectivity diagnostics, media URL resolution, and upload-limit handling.\n- Made file storage work out of the box: fresh installations default to local storage, local mode uses one optional site domain, and official assets are automatically mapped under `/profile/aid/...` without a duplicate CDN field.\n- RocketMQ is now fully disabled by default. MQ dispatch requires both explicit infrastructure enablement and the admin business switch; unconfigured environments do not initialize producers or consumers.\n- Improved error-log processing and error-rule conversion to make provider failure diagnosis and rule maintenance more efficient.\n- Redesigned the project upgrade page with clearer version, updater, release-note, runtime-configuration, and official-asset sections.\n- Expanded the deployment configuration center with separate Docker and non-Docker settings, HTTPS public/admin domains and ports, plus secure certificate-chain and private-key uploads from the admin console.\n- Added individual DNS, certificate, HTTPS, MySQL, Redis, and RocketMQ diagnostics. Certificates are validated for domain coverage, validity, server-auth usage, and key matching before controlled backups are retained.\n- Added a live upgrade/rollback console, phase progress, and the `aid progress` command, with duplicate-task protection across the UI, backend, and installer.\n- Added pre-upgrade CPU and memory detection. Servers with no more than 4 CPU cores or 4 GiB of memory receive a prominent outage-risk and backup confirmation.\n- Fixed a Docker first-install issue that could leave the updater configuration under a temporary directory. Verified legacy configurations are now migrated into the controlled configuration directory with a backup retained.\n- Standardized the backend runtime locale to UTF-8 for Docker and non-Docker deployments, fixing Linux initialization of official assets with Chinese object keys.\n- Improved managed Redis client detection for non-Docker installations and strengthened same-version updater artifact refresh and recovery behavior.\n- Refined episode review rules: the final video and episode description remain required, while the episode cover is optional and validated when supplied.\n- Improved the Web creation workflow, including final preview and publishing, movie/series state isolation, generation-model synchronization, storyboard task recovery after refresh, video-duration detection, subtitle display, and batch-generation parameter filtering.\n- Includes the incremental database script `sql/v1.0.0-beta.3.sql`. The updater applies it through the existing migration history mechanism; back up the database and deployment configuration before upgrading.\n\n\u003e This is a Beta release. Validate model settings, object storage, database migration, and the complete creation workflow in a staging environment before production use.",
